System hardware requirements:
    - Intel Core 2 Duo E6300 / AMD Athlon 64 X2 3800+ or newer (just to execute, recommend newer hardware for smoother experience).
    - At least 50 MB of available system memory.
    - At least 140 MB of available storage.
System software requirements (minimum) 64-bit only:
    - Python 3.6 or newer.
    - Windows 7 Starter, Home Basic, Home Premium, Professional, Enterprise, Ultimate SP1 (Build 7601 or newer with UCRT patch via update KB2999226 and the Visual C++ 2015–2019 Redistributable (x64) runtimes) 
    - Linux Kernel 2.6.13+ 
    - macOS X 10.9 (Mavericks)
    - You must install the required libraries for the utility to work, you can install them with this command: 
    'pip install -r requirements.txt' or 'pip3 install -r requirements.txt'.

Attention: When you want to use the utility, execute file 'run.py' with Python 3.6+ or 'python run.py' / 'python3 run.py'. 

If you want to enable Debug mode, add the --debug flag, for example 'python/python3 run.py --debug', 
although events with severity higher than 'INFO' will be automatically logged.